  "final_resolution": "### Single Most Important Trade-Off:\nThe most critical trade-off in this decision is between **initial cost and flexibility**. Building a custom CRM in-house offers higher flexibility and a perfect fit to specific sales processes, but comes with a significantly higher initial cost. Licensing a SaaS CRM, on the other hand, has a lower initial cost but may require more manual workarounds to meet all business needs.\n\n### Recommendation:\n**BUILD a custom CRM in-house.**\n\n### Justification:\nWhile the SaaS CRM option offers a lower initial cost and covers 80% of requirements out of the box, the remaining 20% would need manual workaround processes, which could be inefficient and costly in the long run. The Jiss Tech tool and other sources indicate that the initial development cost for a custom CRM is higher but becomes more cost-effective after 18-36 months. Given the significant flexibility and alignment with specific sales processes, the long-term benefits of a custom CRM outweigh the higher initial investment for the company in question.",
  "history_entry_count": 6
